silm:instances_papers_02_music_sections_03_olog_node_arrow_law_yoneda_hom_leg silm:hasExample "In '03OlognodearrowlawYonedaHomLeg', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, In the Music graph engine entry section 03_olog_node_arrow_law, the '] \\& |[terminalnode]| TraceWitness tikzcd% The olog diagram law for Manifest and TaskNode: the Manifest profiles the TaskNode (top) and witnesses the source (left); both paths must agree at the TraceWitness (right and bottom).fig:music-olog-manifest-task Diagram law (Figure~fig:music-olog-manifest-task): the olog square commutes when the manifest's profile and witness arrows are consistent; a manifest that does not witness the source that the task node claims cannot produce a valid trace. [0.88]% tikzcd[column sep=large,row sep=large,ampersand replacement=\\&] |[schemanode]| SourceText [r, arrow witnesses the Mittens microchip-id arrow witnessing identifier-by-leg, distinct from identifier-as-Mittens.; also, In the Music graph engine entry section 03_olog_node_arrow_law, the ] \\& |[schemanode]| TypedClaim [d, arrow witnesses the DomesticCat classification arrow as a typed source leg into D_Mittens — NOT an identity onto Mittens." .
